+## 5B. Google Play — Reviewer Notes
+
+Use this if Google Play review asks how the Android blocking flow works.
+
+### Ready-to-paste version
+CEO OS is a personal focus and self-control app.
+
+On Android, the app uses Accessibility to detect when a selected distracting app or supported website is opened, Usage Access to evaluate real time spent on selected apps and supported websites for daily limits, and overlay permission to present the blocking shield when a blocked target is opened.
+
+The Android permission flow is user-initiated and presented progressively. The app does not ask for all system settings at once. It first explains why the permissions are needed, then routes the user to the next missing Android protection setting.
+
+Android website blocking depends on what supported browsers expose through the accessibility tree, so the app does not claim universal website blocking across all Android browsers or web views.
+
+CEO OS does not use Accessibility, Usage Access, or overlay for ads, hidden UI manipulation, or unrelated analytics.
@@
 ### Accessibility
 CEO OS needs Accessibility to detect selected distracting apps and supported websites and apply blocking on-device.
@@
 ### Overlay
 CEO OS needs overlay permission to display the blocking shield when a restricted app or supported website is opened.
+
+### Android disclosure pattern
+CEO OS explains the purpose of Android protection permissions before sending the user to system settings. The user is then routed to the next missing protection setting, rather than being pushed through all Android settings at once.
